caption: Demon Lords

Demon Lord (Unusual Background, free when acquired in play): You have unlocked your Demon Seed. All of the mortal races that are touched by evil have one. To unlock your demon seed, you must personally kill 10,000 people (beings with higher souls); this must be done in play for player characters, but once done the unusual background is free. Once unlocked, you no longer earn experience through Drives, though you can still take advantage of experience loops and training. You can purchase any demonic traits you desire so long as they are approved by the GM, including the ability to learn Demonic Sorcery natively. You can create Torment Afterlifes with the Gadget limitation (Quintus; coins that contain souls), and anyone you personally slay counts as having been sacrificed to you (see Experience Gain section). You cannot create Rapture afterlives, but you can create holding cells for souls (neutral afterlives). However, you only gain half experience from these actions. On the bright side, you can create minions via the Demonic Minions entry, and anyone they slay counts as a sacrifice to you, with them gaining half experience and you gaining half of all the experience your direct minions earn. This goes all the way up, allowing you to create a pyramid of demonic minions earning you experience. You also gain half of all experience your direct minions earn through torment, as do all of your minions. This means a pentacoin in the hands of anyone who serves you is earning you experience, and any person they slay is sacrificed to you and you gain their soul (but only the indirect experience of the sacrifice). Demon Lords cannot create souls.
